/ActualText (SupTech, short for Supervisory Technology, refers to the use of technology by regulatory authorities \(supervisors\) to improve their oversight and supervision of financial institutions and markets. SupTech aims to enhance regulatory effectiveness, efficiency, and transparency through the use of innovative tools, data analytics, and automation.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Overall, SupTech plays a crucial role in modernizing regulatory practices, strengthening financial supervision, and promoting financial stability and integrity in global markets. As regulatory requirements continue to evolve and become more complex, the adoption of SupTech is expected to increase, driving greater efficiency, transparency, and resilience in the financial system.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
